language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ cur_num: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ The number 48 has this peculiarity: adding 1 to it gives a square number, and adding 1 to its half also gives a square number. Find another number with this peculiarity between 1 and 10000.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/cur_num.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ peculiar: a number between 1 and 10000, other than 48, with the peculiarity
letting limit = 10000
find peculiar : int(1..limit)
$ root1: the square root of peculiar + 1 (at most 101, since 101 * 101 > limit + 1)
letting root_limit = 101
find root1 : int(1..root_limit)
$ root2: the square root of peculiar / 2 + 1
find root2 : int(1..root_limit)

branching on [peculiar, root1, root2]

such that
$ the number has an integer half, so it is even
peculiar % 2 = 0,
$ adding 1 to the number gives a square number
peculiar + 1 = root1 * root1,
$ adding 1 to its half gives a square number
peculiar / 2 + 1 = root2 * root2,
$ the number must be another number, not 48
peculiar != 48
